## Type-specific requirements (spec type: {{ spec_type }})

{% if spec_type == 'button' %}
- Variants (primary, secondary, ghost, etc.) must differ in background, border, and color using design tokens.
- Include hover, focus-visible, and disabled states in CSS.
- Use `<button type="button">` as the interactive root.
{% elif spec_type == 'card' %}
- Structure: header, body, and optional footer regions inside a card container.
- Use elevation (border or shadow) and radius from tokens; do not use `<button>` as the root element.
{% elif spec_type == 'navigation' %}
- Use `<nav>` with list semantics (`<ul>` / `<li>` or accessible equivalent).
- Include an active/current state style for one item.
{% elif spec_type == 'input' %}
- Associate `<label>` with `<input>`; support error/disabled visual states using tokens.
{% elif spec_type == 'modal' %}
- Use dialog semantics (role="dialog", labelled title); overlay + panel; focus trap implied in markup comments if needed.
{% elif spec_type == 'layout' or spec_type == 'hero' %}
- Use semantic layout markup (`section`, `header`) appropriate to the component name.
- No button root unless the spec name implies a CTA-only widget.
{% else %}
- Match semantic HTML and layout to type "{{ spec_type }}" and component name {{ component_name }}.
- Do not default to a plain `<button>` unless type is button.
{% endif %}

